L82: #### Searching by Author Name
L83:   * Using the Author(s) field produces best results for author name searches.
L84:   * For the most precise name search, follow surname(s), forename(s) or surname(s), initial(s) pattern: example Hawking, S or Hawking, Stephen
L85:   * For best results on multiple author names, separate individuals with a ; (semicolon). Example: Jin, D S; Ye, J
L86:   * Author names enclosed in quotes will return only exact matches. For example, "Stephen Hawking" will not return matches for Stephen W. Hawking.
L87:   * Diacritic character variants are automatically searched in the Author(s) field.
L88:   * Queries with no punctuation will treat each term independently.
L89: #### Searching by subcategory
L90: 
L91:   * To search within a subcategory select All fields.
L92:   * A subcategory search can be combined with an author or keyword search by clicking on add another term in advanced search.
L93: ## Tips
L94: 
L95: Wildcards:
L96: 
L97:   * Use ? to replace a single character or * to replace any number of characters.
L98:   * Can be used in any field, but not in the first character position. See Journal References tips for exceptions.
L99: 
L100: Expressions:
L101: 
L102:   * TeX expressions can be searched, enclosed in single $ characters.
L103: 
L104: Phrases:
L105: 
L106:   * Enclose phrases in double quotes for exact matches in title, abstract, and comments.
L107: 
L108: Dates:
L109:   * Sorting by announcement date will use the year and month the original version (v1) of the paper was announced.
L110:   * Sorting by submission date will use the year, month and day the latest version of the paper was submitted.
L111: 
L112: Journal References:
L113:   * If a journal reference search contains a wildcard, matches will be made using wildcard matching as expected. For example, math* will match math, maths, mathematics.
L114:   * If a journal reference search does not contain a wildcard, only exact phrases entered will be matched. For example, math would match math or math and science but not maths or mathematics.
L115:   * All journal reference searches that do not contain a wildcard are literal searches: a search for Physica A will match all papers with journal references containing Physica A, but a search for Physica A, 245 (1997) 181 will only return the paper with journal reference Physica A, 245 (1997) 181.
